# Photography originals — ~80,000 files / 5.3 GB.
# Deliberately untracked: git is here to version the site's code and markup,
# not the image archive. The images live on the Azure App Service disk and in
# the local OneDrive copy.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.JPG
*.JPEG

# ...but the small derived images are part of the site rather than the archive,
# and the deploy runs from a checkout: anything git cannot see, GitHub Actions
# cannot ship. These three sets are generated or hand-made site furniture --
# 240x160 grid thumbnails and page chrome, about 80 MB all told, against 5.3 GB
# of photographs. Tracking them is what makes a deploy able to reproduce the
# site rather than only its markup.
!you/**/thumbnail.jpg
!catalog/**/*.jpg
!images/**/*.jpg
!images/**/*.jpeg

# FrontPage Server Extensions binary databases (1pvt/) — 140 MB, dead.
*.btr
*.lck

# Windows / editor noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp
~$*

# Node tooling. Nothing in tools/ has runtime dependencies — packages only ever
# get installed here for one-off checks — but an accidental `npm install` should
# never be able to add thousands of files to a commit.
node_modules/

# Deploy scratch. The workflow builds _deploy-config/ and _deploy-images/ on the
# runner when shipping web.config or the thumbnails ahead of the pages, and
# FTP-Deploy-Action keeps a manifest per scope of what is already on the server.
_deploy-config/
_deploy-images/
.ftp-deploy-*.json
.ftp-deploy-sync-state.json

# scratch commit-message file used by the tooling
.commitmsg
